# Build-context exclusions for console/Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` in the build stage copies the DEVELOPER'S
# node_modules over the one the deps stage just installed — so the image is
# built against whatever platform the host happens to be (a Windows or macOS
# tree lands in a linux/amd64 image, native bindings and all) instead of the
# clean `npm ci` result. Excluding it is what makes the deps stage mean
# anything. Everything else here is either build output that gets regenerated,
# or must never reach an image at all.

# Reinstalled by the deps stage via `npm ci` — never ship the host's copy.
node_modules

# Next.js build output (this repo's next.config.ts sets distDir .next-build).
# Regenerated by `npm run build`; copying a stale one in only risks confusing it.
.next
.next-build
# Stray/alternate build dirs from parallel local builds and tooling runs.
.next-build-*

# Secrets must never enter the image or its layer history. The console reads
# its config from the runtime environment, never from a baked file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control + local tooling noise.
.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Tests and coverage add build-context weight and nothing to the runtime image.
coverage
